# RTL8852BS2 association: ask one real access point to associate this host and
# require its Association Response back.
#
# The parent is the station-join profile whose whole chain already passed on the
# board, so one run of this image re-validates everything proven before -
# firmware download, the runtime control plane, the no-link role and CAM, the
# passive 2.4 GHz 1-13 sweep with real Beacon RX, the wlan0 netdev whose wapi
# scan reports those access points, the Probe Request/Response exchange, the
# directed Authentication Request/Response, and the JOININFO + ADDR_CAM_UPDATE
# that tell the firmware and the hardware this host is a station in that BSS -
# and then adds the one new frame.
#
# That frame is the Association Request. It carries the capability information
# an 802.11ax part honestly has (ESS, short preamble, short slot time, and the
# Privacy bit echoing the target's), a listen interval of one beacon, the SSID,
# the same two rate elements the Probe Request advertises and, for a target that
# advertises Privacy, an RSN element naming CCMP as the pairwise and group
# cipher and the pre-shared key suite. That one suite is all this port can name,
# so an access point requiring anything else is skipped rather than asked, and a
# run with nothing else in range reports EOPNOTSUPP.
#
# Authentication and association go out inside one sweep. IEEE 802.11 clause
# 11.3 accepts an Association Request only while the access point still holds
# this host in state 2 from its Authentication Response, so the request is
# transmitted from the receive loop the moment that response is decoded, with
# the radio still parked on the target's channel by the scan-offload dwell.
#
# Up to two attempts are made, differing only in the SSID: first what the
# target advertised - zero length included, which is the only SSID there is
# evidence for - and then, when the target suppressed its SSID and the first
# attempt did not associate, the SSID of a sibling BSS on the same channel
# whose BSSID differs only in the first octet. That second one is a labelled
# guess and every line it produces says ssid-source=sibling.
#
# An answered exchange is the result whatever status code it carries. Only
# status 0 with a non-zero association identifier prints the completion line,
# and only then are the two connect commands re-sent with that identifier, in
# the vendor order (JOININFO, then ADDR_CAM_UPDATE), followed by a confirming
# sweep that must still receive the target's Beacons.
#
# This is not a link. No key is installed, no data frame is sent or received,
# no wlan0 behaviour changes, no IP address is configured, and the port's TSF is
# still frozen because mac_port_init() is not ported yet. This profile runs no
# four-way handshake; wireless_wpa_diag is the profile that does. Still
# RAM-only: nothing written to eMMC, SPI flash, eFuse or the U-Boot
# environment.

#include "../wireless_join_diag/defconfig"

CONFIG_K1_RTL8852BS2_RUNTIME_ASSOC_DIAGNOSTIC=y
